# Messages the file mailer writes in development, and CVs the file store
# writes. Correspondence and other people's documents, and not something to
# commit.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, and that is not tidiness. Written bare as
# "mail/" the rule matches a directory of that name ANYWHERE in the tree — and
# because git on Windows has core.ignoreCase set, it matched src/.../Mail/ as
# well. The entire mail feature, source and tests, was therefore invisible to
# git for weeks while commits went in that claimed to add it. A clean clone did
# not compile.
#
# These paths are where the File transports actually write, relative to the
# content root. Anything else called Mail is source.
/mail/
/src/JiranisokoTech.Web/mail/
/cvs/
/src/JiranisokoTech.Web/cvs/
/documents/
/src/JiranisokoTech.Web/documents/

# Worktrees the agent tooling creates. Not part of the project.
.claude/worktrees/
